---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Project from '../components/Project.astro';

import Fog1 from '../../assets/bsk/fog-1.png'
import Fog2 from '../../assets/bsk/fog-2.png'

import Dibella1 from '../../assets/bsk/dibella-1.png'
import Dibella2 from '../../assets/bsk/dibella-2.png'

import Divorce1 from '../../assets/bsk/divorced-1.png'
import Divorce2 from '../../assets/bsk/divorced-2.png'

---
<Layout>
  <main>
    <h2>Beyond Skyrim: Cyrodiil</h2>
    <p>
      My contributions to <a href="https://beyondskyrim.org/project/cyrodiil">Beyond Skyrim Cyrodiil</a>
      a collaborative project to recreate Cyrodiil in the time and setting of Skyrim, along with writeups
      from various members of the PR team.
    </p>
    <Project
      id="fog"
      title="Fog at Varinius"
      images={[
        { src: Fog1, alt: "A stone fortification and bridge viewed from outside an heavy fog" },
        { src: Fog2, alt: "A stone fortification and bridge viewed from within an extreme" },
      ]}
    >
      <p slot="summary">
        The Varinius Border Passage is one of many well-maintained border gates
        across the Imperial Province. With it being staffed by the soldiers of the
        Empire; it protects and ensures the stability of Cyrodiil's border with
        Valenwood. Lately, however, deep fog has become a persistent problem for
        the soldiers of the gate, to the point that rumours now circulate an
        unnatural cause for this disturbance. Furthermore, rumours have circulated
        that the unknown actors involved may be associated with a local Dominion
        presence. Whatever the cause, it can only be resolved by exploring and
        deciding how to finally address the unexpected phenomenon. This
        miscellaneous quest was implemented by Kieran Knowles and written by Rhea
        and Linton. -- <a href="https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/images/313801">The Cyrodiil Team</a>
      </p>
    </Project>
    <Project
      id='dibella'
      title='A Case of Dibellan Arts'
      images={[
        { src: Dibella1, alt: "A man walking into a chapel chamber while talking" },
        { src: Dibella2, alt: "A man kneeling down to pet a spider while praising it" },
      ]}
    >
      <p slot="summary">
        The love found across Tamriel has never been in question by the priests
        of Dibella; though some forms of love can even bring pause to those in
        Anvil's chapel. Priest Erronius has seemingly become smitten by a spider
        named Charlotte. What is more is that another Priest of Dibella is
        trying to invite him over to teach her about Dibella's Lily. How are
        these two events connected, and why has a Priest of Dibella fallen for a
        spider? When adventurers reach the Chapel of Dibella in Anvil, they can
        discover the answers to these questions in the miscellaneous quest
        "A Case of Dibellan Arts" written by the Anvil team and implemented by
        Kieran Knowles. -- <a href="https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/images/302874">The Cyrodiil Team</a>
      </p>
    </Project>
    <Project
      id='divorced'
      title='Divorced'
      images={[
        { src: Divorce1, alt: "A man and a woman sitting on a bench in the evening" },
        { src: Divorce2, alt: "A man and a woman hugging in a castle hall" },
      ]}
    >
      <p slot="summary">
        The challenges of divorce can often find themselves turning up even after
        a couple has parted ways, some believing that second chances are still
        possible, but others might not see it that way. When adventurers explore
        Anvil, they can help Darcine Lorierre who is concerned about her
        ex-husband. He is seeking her out following his time in prison, which
        explains Darcine's worries. Adventurers can seek to put her mind at ease
        and resolve the chance of an unwanted reunion through various manners.
        What will be the final outcome, and will it involve this fated reunion?
        That is yet to be seen.

        The Divorced quest is one of many miscellaneous quests found in Anvil and
        was written by Deagler and implemented by Kieran Knowles. -- <a href="https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/images/300451">The Cyrodiil Team</a>
      </p>
    </Project>
   </main>
</Layout>
